<title>INDIA: DELHI SHARES END LOWER ON FOREIGN SELLING.</title>
<headline>DELHI SHARES END LOWER ON FOREIGN SELLING.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delhi stocks closed lower on Wednesday on selling by foreign investors and speculators after the stock market regulator, the Securities and Exchange Board of India, deferred a decision to introduce easier carry-forward rules.</p>
<p>The Delhi Stock Exchange's benchmark index closed 8.36 points lower at 922.90 points.</p>
